{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":" suitable prebuilt path is available, the app may build or prepare only the NFCorpus index.\\n\\n### Real Command Execution\\n- Use real Anserini commands for setup, search, and evaluation.\\n- Do NOT hardcode or mock: search results, run files, qrels, scores, or expected metrics.\\n\\n### Search Backend\\n- Backend must support live query search over NFCorpus.\\n- Implementation may use Anserini REST server or CLI-backed search endpoint.\\n- Must be backed by Anserini, not a custom search implementation.\\n- Search results must include: rank, document id, score, and document content/snippet text.\\n\\n### BM25 Evaluation Workflow\\nThe app must:\\n1. Run `SearchCollection` or the reproduction-provided equivalent command\\n2. Write a TREC-format run file\\n3. Evaluate with the appropriate Anserini/TrecEval command\\n4. Parse observed metric values\\n5. Compare observed values with the reproduction-provided expected values when available\\n\\n### Cached Evaluation Option\\n- If live evaluation is too slow for hosted use, the app may run evaluation during setup/startup and expose a browser \\\"Verify/Rerun\\\" action that reuses cached NFCorpus artifacts.\\n- The UI must clearly distinguish cached setup results from a fresh rerun.\\n\\n### Status/Readiness Panel\\nShow a readiness panel with","partial":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me write my own neutral restatement of the PRD.\n","thinkingSignature":"b53b0ff6e98f244cd85d5f7f41ae3bd1eb508eb9102cb5d09e8b5cedff8a1417"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_390tyjndi6pq_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench\n\n## Project Overview\n\nBuild a single Dockerized web application deployable on Render that provides live NFCorpus retrieval diagnostics powered by Anserini. The application must let users search NFCorpus in real time, observe how the dataset was prepared using Anserini skills, and verify whether Anserini's observed BM25 evaluation metrics match the expected reproduction targets. The scope is intentionally limited to NFCorpus only—no full BEIR download, no general-purpose retrieval dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nAnserini's retrieval evaluation workflow is spread across skill documentation, CLI commands, run files, qrels, evaluator output, and deployment concerns. Researchers and developers need a small, hosted, self-contained demo that makes a real IR workflow fully inspectable: live search, dataset preparation, and observed-vs-expected evaluation metrics—all visible in a browser.\n\n---\n\n## Users\n\n| Persona | Need |\n|---|---|\n| IR researchers | Small live retrieval-quality demo |\n| Anserini developers | Validate NFCorpus setup and evaluation workflows |\n| Demo viewers | Compare live search results with measured retrieval metrics |\n| Operators | Deploy benchmark outputs to Render |\n\n---\n\n## Goals (What the App Must Do)\n\n1. **Use repo-local Anserini skills** as the authoritative source for setup, CLI syntax, reproduction discovery, search, and evaluation commands.\n2. **Deploy as a single Render Docker web service.**\n3. **Use NFCorpus as the sole dataset**—no other BEIR corpora.\n4. **Live query search** over NFCorpus via an Anserini-backed backend (REST server or CLI-backed endpoint).\n5. **Run or verify a BM25 evaluation** using real Anserini commands and qrels.\n6. **Show expected vs. observed metrics**, deltas, commands, and artifact paths in the browser.\n7. **Browser-driven verification** proving no mocked search or mocked evaluation results.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Goals (What the App Must NOT Do)\n\n- Support all BEIR datasets or download the full BEIR corpus archive\n- MS MARCO or other large-corpus demos\n- Dense retrieval, neural reranking, or model training\n- User accounts, authentication, or multi-user job management\n- Custom retrieval engines\n- Use `GetDocument` when search results already include useful document content\n- Require Vercel deployment\n\n---\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n### Skill Dependencies\nThe app must consult these repo-local skills before constructing any commands:\n- `install-anserini-fatjar`\n- `anserini-cli`\n- `anserini-reproduction`\n\n### Fatjar Setup\n- Locate or install an Anserini fatjar and verify it using the skill's runtime checks.\n- Store the verification command in the UI.\n\n### Reproduction Discovery\n- Discover NFCorpus-related reproduction support using the Anserini reproduction workflow.\n- Use reproduction listing/show/dry-run behavior where available to identify:\n  - NFCorpus setup commands\n  - Expected metrics\n  - qrels/eval keys\n  - Setup requirements\n\n### Dataset Scope\n- Any download or cache step must be NFCorpus-specific and documented in the UI.\n- Do not download all BEIR corpora.\n\n### Artifact Preference\n- Prefer a prebuilt/cached NFCorpus index or NFCorpus-specific artifact when Anserini exposes one.\n- If no suitable prebuilt path is available, the app may build or prepare only the NFCorpus index.\n\n### Real Command Execution\n- Use real Anserini commands for setup, search, and evaluation.\n- Do NOT hardcode or mock: search results, run files, qrels, scores, or expected metrics.\n\n### Search Backend\n- Backend must support live query search over NFCorpus.\n- Implementation may use Anserini REST server or CLI-backed search endpoint.\n- Must be backed by Anserini, not a custom search implementation.\n- Search results must include: rank, document id, score, and document content/snippet text.\n\n### BM25 Evaluation Workflow\nThe app must:\n1. Run `SearchCollection` or the reproduction-provided equivalent command\n2. Write a TREC-format run file\n3. Evaluate with the appropriate Anserini/TrecEval command\n4. Parse observed metric values\n5. Compare observed values with the reproduction-provided expected values when available\n\n### Cached Evaluation Option\n- If live evaluation is too slow for hosted use, the app may run evaluation during setup/startup and expose a browser \"Verify/Rerun\" action that reuses cached NFCorpus artifacts.\n- The UI must clearly distinguish cached setup results from a fresh rerun.\n\n### Status/Readiness Panel\nShow a readiness panel with"},"partialJson":"{\"content\":\"# NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\nBuild a single Dockerized web application deployable on Render that provides live NFCorpus retrieval diagnostics powered by Anserini. The application must let users search NFCorpus in real time, observe how the dataset was prepared using Anserini skills, and verify whether Anserini's observed BM25 evaluation metrics match the expected reproduction targets. The scope is intentionally limited to NFCorpus only—no full BEIR download, no general-purpose retrieval dashboard.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nAnserini's retrieval evaluation workflow is spread across skill documentation, CLI commands, run files, qrels, evaluator output, and deployment concerns. Researchers and developers need a small, hosted, self-contained demo that makes a real IR workflow fully inspectable: live search, dataset preparation, and observed-vs-expected evaluation metrics—all visible in a browser.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Users\\n\\n| Persona | Need |\\n|---|---|\\n| IR researchers | Small live retrieval-quality demo |\\n| Anserini developers | Validate NFCorpus setup and evaluation workflows |\\n| Demo viewers | Compare live search results with measured retrieval metrics |\\n| Operators | Deploy benchmark outputs to Render |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Goals (What the App Must Do)\\n\\n1. **Use repo-local Anserini skills** as the authoritative source for setup, CLI syntax, reproduction discovery, search, and evaluation commands.\\n2. **Deploy as a single Render Docker web service.**\\n3. **Use NFCorpus as the sole dataset**—no other BEIR corpora.\\n4. **Live query search** over NFCorpus via an Anserini-backed backend (REST server or CLI-backed endpoint).\\n5. **Run or verify a BM25 evaluation** using real Anserini commands and qrels.\\n6. **Show expected vs. observed metrics**, deltas, commands, and artifact paths in the browser.\\n7. **Browser-driven verification** proving no mocked search or mocked evaluation results.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Non-Goals (What the App Must NOT Do)\\n\\n- Support all BEIR datasets or download the full BEIR corpus archive\\n- MS MARCO or other large-corpus demos\\n- Dense retrieval, neural reranking, or model training\\n- User accounts, authentication, or multi-user job management\\n- Custom retrieval engines\\n- Use `GetDocument` when search results already include useful document content\\n- Require Vercel deployment\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Core Requirements\\n\\n### Skill Dependencies\\nThe app must consult these repo-local skills before constructing any commands:\\n- `install-anserini-fatjar`\\n- `anserini-cli`\\n- `anserini-reproduction`\\n\\n### Fatjar Setup\\n- Locate or install an Anserini fatjar and verify it using the skill's runtime checks.\\n- Store the verification command in the UI.\\n\\n### Reproduction Discovery\\n- Discover NFCorpus-related reproduction support using the Anserini reproduction workflow.\\n- Use reproduction listing/show/dry-run behavior where available to identify:\\n  - NFCorpus setup commands\\n  - Expected metrics\\n  - qrels/eval keys\\n  - Setup requirements\\n\\n### Dataset Scope\\n- Any download or cache step must be NFCorpus-specific and documented in the UI.\\n- Do not download all BEIR corpora.\\n\\n### Artifact Preference\\n- Prefer a prebuilt/cached NFCorpus index or NFCorpus-specific artifact when Anserini exposes one.\\n- If no suitable prebuilt path is available, the app may build or prepare only the NFCorpus index.\\n\\n### Real Command Execution\\n- Use real Anserini commands for setup, search, and evaluation.\\n- Do NOT hardcode or mock: search results, run files, qrels, scores, or expected metrics.\\n\\n### Search Backend\\n- Backend must support live query search over NFCorpus.\\n- Implementation may use Anserini REST server or CLI-backed search endpoint.\\n- Must be backed by Anserini, not a custom search implementation.\\n- Search results must include: rank, document id, score, and document content/snippet text.\\n\\n### BM25 Evaluation Workflow\\nThe app must:\\n1. Run `SearchCollection` or the reproduction-provided equivalent command\\n2. Write a TREC-format run file\\n3. Evaluate with the appropriate Anserini/TrecEval command\\n4. Parse observed metric values\\n5. Compare observed values with the reproduction-provided expected values when available\\n\\n### Cached Evaluation Option\\n- If live evaluation is too slow for hosted use, the app may run evaluation during setup/startup and expose a browser \\\"Verify/Rerun\\\" action that reuses cached NFCorpus artifacts.\\n- The UI must clearly distinguish cached setup results from a fresh rerun.\\n\\n### Status/Readiness Panel\\nShow a readiness panel with","index":1}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":4349,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":4349,"cost":{"input":0.0013047,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0013047}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780603838901,"responseId":"06710ebe7ddea34b6601e34fedaab637"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me write my own neutral restatement of the PRD.\n","thinkingSignature":"b53b0ff6e98f244cd85d5f7f41ae3bd1eb508eb9102cb5d09e8b5cedff8a1417"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_390tyjndi6pq_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench\n\n## Project Overview\n\nBuild a single Dockerized web application deployable on Render that provides live NFCorpus retrieval diagnostics powered by Anserini. The application must let users search NFCorpus in real time, observe how the dataset was prepared using Anserini skills, and verify whether Anserini's observed BM25 evaluation metrics match the expected reproduction targets. The scope is intentionally limited to NFCorpus only—no full BEIR download, no general-purpose retrieval dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nAnserini's retrieval evaluation workflow is spread across skill documentation, CLI commands, run files, qrels, evaluator output, and deployment concerns. Researchers and developers need a small, hosted, self-contained demo that makes a real IR workflow fully inspectable: live search, dataset preparation, and observed-vs-expected evaluation metrics—all visible in a browser.\n\n---\n\n## Users\n\n| Persona | Need |\n|---|---|\n| IR researchers | Small live retrieval-quality demo |\n| Anserini developers | Validate NFCorpus setup and evaluation workflows |\n| Demo viewers | Compare live search results with measured retrieval metrics |\n| Operators | Deploy benchmark outputs to Render |\n\n---\n\n## Goals (What the App Must Do)\n\n1. **Use repo-local Anserini skills** as the authoritative source for setup, CLI syntax, reproduction discovery, search, and evaluation commands.\n2. **Deploy as a single Render Docker web service.**\n3. **Use NFCorpus as the sole dataset**—no other BEIR corpora.\n4. **Live query search** over NFCorpus via an Anserini-backed backend (REST server or CLI-backed endpoint).\n5. **Run or verify a BM25 evaluation** using real Anserini commands and qrels.\n6. **Show expected vs. observed metrics**, deltas, commands, and artifact paths in the browser.\n7. **Browser-driven verification** proving no mocked search or mocked evaluation results.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Goals (What the App Must NOT Do)\n\n- Support all BEIR datasets or download the full BEIR corpus archive\n- MS MARCO or other large-corpus demos\n- Dense retrieval, neural reranking, or model training\n- User accounts, authentication, or multi-user job management\n- Custom retrieval engines\n- Use `GetDocument` when search results already include useful document content\n- Require Vercel deployment\n\n---\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n### Skill Dependencies\nThe app must consult these repo-local skills before constructing any commands:\n- `install-anserini-fatjar`\n- `anserini-cli`\n- `anserini-reproduction`\n\n### Fatjar Setup\n- Locate or install an Anserini fatjar and verify it using the skill's runtime checks.\n- Store the verification command in the UI.\n\n### Reproduction Discovery\n- Discover NFCorpus-related reproduction support using the Anserini reproduction workflow.\n- Use reproduction listing/show/dry-run behavior where available to identify:\n  - NFCorpus setup commands\n  - Expected metrics\n  - qrels/eval keys\n  - Setup requirements\n\n### Dataset Scope\n- Any download or cache step must be NFCorpus-specific and documented in the UI.\n- Do not download all BEIR corpora.\n\n### Artifact Preference\n- Prefer a prebuilt/cached NFCorpus index or NFCorpus-specific artifact when Anserini exposes one.\n- If no suitable prebuilt path is available, the app may build or prepare only the NFCorpus index.\n\n### Real Command Execution\n- Use real Anserini commands for setup, search, and evaluation.\n- Do NOT hardcode or mock: search results, run files, qrels, scores, or expected metrics.\n\n### Search Backend\n- Backend must support live query search over NFCorpus.\n- Implementation may use Anserini REST server or CLI-backed search endpoint.\n- Must be backed by Anserini, not a custom search implementation.\n- Search results must include: rank, document id, score, and document content/snippet text.\n\n### BM25 Evaluation Workflow\nThe app must:\n1. Run `SearchCollection` or the reproduction-provided equivalent command\n2. Write a TREC-format run file\n3. Evaluate with the appropriate Anserini/TrecEval command\n4. Parse observed metric values\n5. Compare observed values with the reproduction-provided expected values when available\n\n### Cached Evaluation Option\n- If live evaluation is too slow for hosted use, the app may run evaluation during setup/startup and expose a browser \"Verify/Rerun\" action that reuses cached NFCorpus artifacts.\n- The UI must clearly distinguish cached setup results from a fresh rerun.\n\n### Status/Readiness Panel\nShow a readiness panel with"},"partialJson":"{\"content\":\"# NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\nBuild a single Dockerized web application deployable on Render that provides live NFCorpus retrieval diagnostics powered by Anserini. The application must let users search NFCorpus in real time, observe how the dataset was prepared using Anserini skills, and verify whether Anserini's observed BM25 evaluation metrics match the expected reproduction targets. The scope is intentionally limited to NFCorpus only—no full BEIR download, no general-purpose retrieval dashboard.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\n\\nAnserini's retrieval evaluation workflow is spread across skill documentation, CLI commands, run files, qrels, evaluator output, and deployment concerns. Researchers and developers need a small, hosted, self-contained demo that makes a real IR workflow fully inspectable: live search, dataset preparation, and observed-vs-expected evaluation metrics—all visible in a browser.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Users\\n\\n| Persona | Need |\\n|---|---|\\n| IR researchers | Small live retrieval-quality demo |\\n| Anserini developers | Validate NFCorpus setup and evaluation workflows |\\n| Demo viewers | Compare live search results with measured retrieval metrics |\\n| Operators | Deploy benchmark outputs to Render |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Goals (What the App Must Do)\\n\\n1. **Use repo-local Anserini skills** as the authoritative source for setup, CLI syntax, reproduction discovery, search, and evaluation commands.\\n2. **Deploy as a single Render Docker web service.**\\n3. **Use NFCorpus as the sole dataset**—no other BEIR corpora.\\n4. **Live query search** over NFCorpus via